BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[SSF] Sign Hill Stewards: Habitat Restoration
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T120000
DTSTAMP:20260821T134431Z
UID:flowstobay-17603-1791622800-1791633600@flowstobay.org@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Many rare plant and animal species live on Sign Hill’s nativ
 e grasslands\, including the endangered mission blue butterfly. Help us co
 nserve and restore their habitat by installing native plants and removing 
 invasive plants! Sign Hill Stewards will do important work while also lear
 ning more about the wildlife in their backyard. \n  \nWhen: Every other 
 Friday from 9am-12pm and the 2nd Saturday of each month from 9am-12pm. Onl
 y cancelled for heavy rains. \nWhere: Volunteers will park at the Sign Hi
 ll Parking Lot nearby 964 Ridgeview Ct\, South San Francisco\, CA (Google 
 Maps Link) and hike with staff to the restoration site. \nRegistration: R
 egistration is required. Volunteers under the age of 18 must have a youth 
 waiver signed by a parent/guardian. Youth under the age of 15 are welcome 
 and must be accompanied by an adult. \nWhat to bring: To prepare for work
 ing outdoors\, please bring work gloves\, plenty of water\, sturdy shoes\,
  long pants and sleeves\, a hat/sunscreen\, and a completed waiver for e
 ach volunteer. Volunteers should expect some hiking on steep terrain. \nRE
 GISTER HERE\n\nAges: Varies per event — many family-friendly. Confirm wi
 th event host.\nSource: https://flowstobay.org/calendar/sign-hill-stewards
 -habitat-restoration-2026-10-10/\nLast synced: 2026-08-21 06:44 PDT
LOCATION:Sign Hill Parking Lot\, 964 Ridgeview Ct\, South San Francisco\, 
 CA\, 94080\, United States
URL:https://flowstobay.org/calendar/sign-hill-stewards-habitat-restoration
 -2026-10-10/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[SM] The HEAL Project Community Farm Day
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T120000
DTSTAMP:20260821T134431Z
UID:flowstobay-17537-1791622800-1791633600@flowstobay.org@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Now offering Community Farm Days! Gatherings are held on the
  second Saturday of the month from 9am-12pm\, Year-round. Heavy rain can
 cels\, we will go forward as planned if the day calls for light rain.  Ch
 eck our social media or email farmer@thehealproject.org if you want to che
 ck on the status of this event in the winter time. Please note the minimu
 m age for youth to volunteer is 10. We ask that supporters RSVP to this ev
 ent\, so please do not RSVP unless you are reasonably certain you will be 
 able to attend so that others do not miss out.   \nWear clothes you don
 ’t mind working in. Help us harvest fruits\, veggies and flowers\, sprea
 d compost\, plant seedlings or remove weeds – prepare to get your hands 
 dirty! To minimize health risks\, we ask that all attendees wear masks and
  bring their own clippers\, work gloves\, water bottles\, sunscreen\, hats
 \, etc. We will be practicing social distancing. \nThe San Mateo County S
 chool Farm is located at the end of Bridgeport Drive in Half Moon Bay (in
  the Princeton by the Sea neighborhood). Please park vehicles in front of 
 the public park at 300 Bridgeport Drive\, Half Moon Bay. Continue walking 
 on Bridgeport drive until it dead ends (about 3 blocks) where you will see
  a small sign for The HEAL Project. Follow the footpath through the trees
  to arrive at the farm! \nPlease leave dogs at home- we love them\, but t
 hey are not allowed at the farm. \nRSVP HERE \nPLEASE MAKE SURE TO SIGN OU
 R REQUIRED WAIVER\n\nAges: Varies per event — many family-friendly. Conf
 irm with event host.\nSource: https://flowstobay.org/calendar/the-heal-pro
 ject-community-farm-day-2026-10-10/\nLast synced: 2026-08-21 06:44 PDT
LOCATION:San Mateo County School Farm\, 500 Bridgeport Drive\, Half Moon B
 ay\, CA\, 94019\, United States
URL:https://flowstobay.org/calendar/the-heal-project-community-farm-day-20
 26-10-10/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[PAC] San Pedro Valley Park: Trail and Habitat Restoration Work Da
 ys
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T120000
DTSTAMP:20260821T134431Z
UID:flowstobay-17538-1791622800-1791633600@flowstobay.org@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Trail and Habitat Restoration Work Days \nEach month\, the se
 cond Saturday is designated for Trail Work and the third Saturday is 
 designated for Habitat Restoration Work. Volunteers meet at the Visitor C
 enter at 9 a.m. for Trail work and and 10 am for Habitat restoration t
 o begin work with rangers and/or volunteer leaders. Tools are provided. On
 ly gloves and other personal protective items (e.g.\, masks) are needed by
  volunteers.  Trail work typically involves clearing brush from the tra
 il sides\, cleaning out drain dips\, raking out trail bends\, and cutting 
 overhanging branches. Habitat Restoration often involves removing invasi
 ve plants (like the ever-present thistle) from trailside areas\, maintaini
 ng the Native Plant Garden at the Visitor Center\, or planting new vegetat
 ion. These work parties typically last about 3 hours\, i.e.\, until noon o
 r 1 pm. \nIf you are interested in joining us\, or just learning more abou
 t what we do\, please call (650-355-5454) or email us (friendsofsanpedrova
 lley@gmail.com) and we’ll be happy to talk with you. Or just drop by the
  Visitor Center on any weekend day (from 10 am to 4 pm) and speak with one
  of the Friends’ volunteers who are there.\n\nAges: Varies per event —
  many family-friendly. Confirm with event host.\nSource: https://flowstoba
 y.org/calendar/san-pedro-valley-park-trail-and-habitat-restoration-work-da
 ys-2026-10-10/\nLast synced: 2026-08-21 06:44 PDT
LOCATION:San Pedro Valley Park\, 600 Oddstad Blvd\, Pacifica\, CA\, 94044
 \, United States
URL:https://flowstobay.org/calendar/san-pedro-valley-park-trail-and-habita
 t-restoration-work-days-2026-10-10/
END:VEVENT
